{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ac7349f68c9ef655","name":"Providence-Class Destroyer","source":{"id":"source:reference-ac7349f68c9ef655","title":"Providence-Class Destroyer","revision":20026,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:03:22Z","sha256":"cfa5d8e94a9be271a9dd5cef61f647890cf9a68a035321ea4bc583fb8846445d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20026","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Providence-Class%20Destroyer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ac7349f68c9ef655","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Originally built for the Trade Federation by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quarren"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quarren","referenceId":"reference:f032fd9263dbff5e"}," Free Dac Volunteers Engineering Corps, the kilometer-long ",{"tag":"i","children":["Providence"]},"-Class Destroyer (frequently referred to as a \"Trade Federation Cruiser\") is one of the Confederacy's most powerful warships, more than a match for any similarly classed cruiser in the Republic Navy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["It is so formidable in combat that ",{"tag":"a","children":["General Grievous"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/General_Grievous","referenceId":"reference:ff638626530ef283"}," uses one, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Invisible Hand"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Invisible_Hand","referenceId":"reference:c91ef6abc03608ad"},", as his flagship in the assault on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},". Endlessly modifiable (due to modular compartments), the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Providence"]},"-Class Destroyer can be made faster with upgraded ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrives"}," or advanced ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sublight Drives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sublight_Drives"},"; it can be made deadlier by adding weapon battery compartments; it can be made into a light ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," carrier by increasing the size of the hangar bays; or countless other variations.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike many warships, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Providence"]},"-Class Destroyer uses a \"bridge-forward\" setup (rather than a dorsal command tower, as is common with Republic warships such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Acclamator"]},"-Class Assault Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acclamator-Class_Assault_Ship"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Venator"]},"-Class Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Venator-Class_Star_Destroyer","referenceId":"reference:72fe718333867ed5"},"). This setup makes the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Providence"]},"-Class slightly more maneuverable than its Republic counterparts, particularly in atmospheres- although the ship is not equipped for ground landings (being designed, like so many other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quarren"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quarren","referenceId":"reference:f032fd9263dbff5e"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mon Calamari"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mon_Calamari","referenceId":"reference:5b784aed2214627b"}," ships, for water landings).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Providence"]},"-Class Destroyer Statistics (CL 18)"]},"\n",{